RPT#LANG-574: {
 "summary": "HashCodeBuilder append(Object) could be more efficient"
 "description": "See: <http://svn.apache.org/viewvc/commons/proper/lang/trunk/src/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/builder/HashCodeBuilder.java?view=markup>\nIf you use **reflectionHashCode**, you will eventually call **reflectionAppend(Object)** for every field (see lines 859 to 890). There is a long list of *instanceOf* checks for the various types of arrays. My concern is that having an array field is relatively rare, yet the code does 9 if/else checks before computing the *hashCode* for *one* element."
